A||||5||AkursedX||How about this weather!||||1||
Z||000000||AkursedX||11-21-2000||07:34 PM||||Hello all...  <P>1st of all, I live in Buffalo, and once again I guess we made National news because of our weather.  Well let me say this, I have NEVER seen such chaos in my life.  Although I am too young for the Blizzard of '77, I am sure this one is right up there.<P>I have spent the past 2 days shoveling almost non-stop, and when I wasn't shoveling, I was driving in my Dad's brand new Dodge Ram picking up stranded family and friends or helping people get out of the snow.<P>On the roads, there were countless cars abandoned, Buses stuck, Trucks Jackknifed.  Every single street coming out of the city was in a standstill.  All the highways were shut down.  The reason this storm was so bad was because it began right during rush hour and didn't stop for about 6 hours.  We got 24.5 inches in 24 hours, and along with this was a 35mph non-stop wind. <P>It took my mother 11-1/2 hours to get home.  She works 15 miles away.  It took my boss 23 hours to get home from work. She lives maybe 17 miles away.  One of my friends got stuck on the skyway at 3:30 yesterday and she just got home 20 minutes ago!!  She spent most of the morning in a school because the police managed to get a bus to take everyone off the bridge for food and to warm up.  <P>Needless to say, this has been quite an adventure for me, and I haven't slept since Sunday evening, so I think I will go in my garage, give my Fiero a hug  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, and then go to sleep.  But I will say this, in times like this, you really see the good of the community and how we can come together, I don't even know how many times I've said thank you to complete strngers who helped me out.  <P>How about you other Buffalo people?  I know there's a couple of you, have anymore stories to share?  Fformula88?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-21-2000||08:49 PM||||Those of us in Indiana may not have it nearly as bad as you do, but the weather here has changed drastically in the last 2 weeks.  Week before last, it was in the lower 70s.  Now it's spitting snow and we're expecting a high of about 25F tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||11-21-2000||10:57 PM||||It's gu-uh-ten p-p-pretty c-cold a-round he-here too...||||reg||4
Z||000003||FieroLisa||11-21-2000||11:51 PM||||AUGHH I'm scared! On Monday I have to drive up to Canada through Buffalo- what's the weather supposed to be like then- apparently there is just this huge snow storm in Barrie Ont. today...GRRRREAAAAT. We'll see how well the good ol' mercury tracer handles the snow.<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||11-22-2000||01:54 PM||||We'll definietly be cleaned up by monday over here.  Our plow and salter crews here are pretty damn efficient.  I made it to work in almost normal time.  There were still about 50 or so cars that were abandoned all over the road though.  Plus every road has about a 4 inch layer of ice that are beginning to make huge potholes.  I'm glad my Fiero is in winter hibernation, it would have been ripped to shreds in this weather.  I'll leave the winter for my '94 Plymouth Duster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero5||11-22-2000||02:09 PM||||Geeze, and here we all are in New England with nothin but a little chilly breeze once in awhile. :o(||||reg||1
